{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_mqttactor", "label": "MqttActor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Eine abstrakte, subclass-first Basisklasse \u2014 Subscriptions im Konstruktor deklarieren, eingehenden Traffic in onMessage verarbeiten, mit this.publish senden. onReceive ist versiegelt; von aussen bleibt der Actor per ref.tell steuerbar.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_hooks", "label": "MqttActor-Hooks", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "onMessage, onConnected, onDisconnected, onInvalidMessage, onSelfMessage. Eingehende und Lifecycle-Ereignisse werden ueber die Mailbox zugestellt, sodass die Hooks stets auf dem Aktor-Thread laufen und die Reihenfolge pro Verbindung erhalten bleibt.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_mqttoptions", "label": "MqttOptionsType", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_typed_payloads", "label": "Typisierte Payloads", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "MqttPayload dekodiert lazy \u2014 erst bei text() oder entity(). Ein fehlerhaftes Payload wirft MqttDecodeError innerhalb von onMessage, die Basisklasse faengt ihn und leitet an onInvalidMessage weiter (Default: loggen und verwerfen, kein Neustart).", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_codecs", "label": "MQTT-Codecs", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "string- und Uint8Array-Payloads gehen roh raus, jeder andere Wert wird ueber den Codec kodiert (Default mqttJsonCodec). Einen nackten String als JSON-Entity zu publishen erfordert explizites codec().encode(...).", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_external_control", "label": "Externe Steuerung ueber MqttCommand", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Ein subscribe ohne target liefert an das eigene onMessage, mit target fan-outet es. Ein unsubscribe ohne target entfernt nur fremde Targets \u2014 ein externer Controller kann die im Konstruktor deklarierte Subscription der Subklasse nicht stummschalten. Ein eigenes TSelf muss die kind-Werte publish/subscribe/unsubscribe meiden.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_qos_levels", "label": "QoS-Level", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "QoS 1 ist die typische Balance fuer IoT-Telemetrie; QoS 2 nur, wenn Duplikate schaedlich waeren; QoS 0 fuer schnell ueberholte Statusupdates.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_topic_wildcards", "label": "MQTT-Topic-Wildcards", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "+ trifft genau eine Ebene, # mehrere und muss das letzte Segment sein. Ein # an der Wurzel subscribiert jede Nachricht auf dem Broker \u2014 in einem multi-tenant Broker selten gewollt.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_retained_messages", "label": "Retained Messages", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Vom Broker gespeichert und an jeden neuen Subscriber sofort ausgeliefert \u2014 fuer Konfiguration und letzten bekannten Status. Bei normalem Pub/Sub weglassen, sonst haelt der Broker jede alte Nachricht fuer immer sichtbar.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_own_subscription_registry", "label": "Eigene Subscription-Registry des MqttActor", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "MqttActor ist aelter als der Desired-Subscriptions-Mechanismus der Basisklasse und behaelt seine eigene, reichhaltigere Registry \u2014 QoS pro Topic, mehrere Targets pro Pattern, Deathwatch auf jedem \u2014 mit den gleichen Reconnect-Garantien.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_clean_session_needs_stable_client_id", "label": "cleanSession false braucht dieselbe clientId", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Der Broker tracked Subscriptions und gequeuete Nachrichten pro clientId; eine zufaellige clientId pro Connect macht cleanSession: false nutzlos.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_mqttactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_hooks", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_mqttactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_mqttoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_typed_payloads", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_hooks", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_codecs", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_typed_payloads", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_external_control", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_mqttactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_external_control", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_hooks", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_qos_levels", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_mqttoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_topic_wildcards", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_mqttactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/mqtt.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_retained_messages", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_mqtt_mqttactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content